#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hack-box hub agent: the only thing on a box that talks to the session hub.

Runs as root under hackbox-hubagent.service. Design and API:
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-01-session-hub-design.md.

- Watches /run/hackbox/state. When a session starts it reads the attendee's
  name (typed on the welcome screen), registers the session with the hub and
  writes the download URL, the hub's code and a QR image to /run/hackbox for
  the overlay. The session never waits for the hub.
- Every few seconds it sends a heartbeat and runs the commands in the reply.
  Only two are accepted: extend <1..60> and end. The hub never connects to
  the box, so a hub compromise can extend or end a session, nothing else.
- After the reset archived ~/project it uploads the archive. Jobs are files in
  /var/lib/hackbox/hub/jobs and are retried with backoff, across reboots.
- Token usage: during a session (at most once a minute, every 15 s on the
  time-up screen) it copies the attendee's OpenCode database to a root-only
  temp dir, sums the assistant messages' tokens from the copy (never the live
  file), deletes the copy and sends the totals with the heartbeat.
- Agent keys and the offered agents are set on the hub dashboard. When the hub's
  config_version differs from the one applied here and the box is idle (never
  during a session), it fetches them, writes them with `hackbox secret set` and
  `hackbox agents set`, and resets the welcome screen so it shows them.

Without /etc/hackbox/hub.conf it does nothing. Python 3 standard library only.
Paths are overridable by environment for the tests (HB_*).
"""

